    "description": "American Student Transportation Partners provides outsourced school transportation services for K-12 districts in the United States. The platform serves school districts through route-based, contracted operations using a large fleet of buses and vans rather than passenger-demand or asset-light logistics models. Its business is asset-heavy because service delivery depends on owned or controlled vehicles, depots, drivers, and local operating systems. CVC DIF announced in 2025 that ASTP transported more than 90,000 students each school year across the Northeast and Midwest through a fleet of more than 2,300 vehicles and contracts with over 50 districts. CVC DIF also stated that it had agreed to acquire ASTP from Access Holdings through DIF Infrastructure VII, and public sources reviewed do not disclose the final post-closing ownership structure.",
