    "description": "American Student Transportation Partners (ASTP) provides contracted K-12 student transportation through traditional school-bus routes and alternative and special-needs transportation. It serves school districts through route-based operations supported by vehicles, depots, drivers and local operating systems. At the August 2025 transaction announcement, ASTP transported more than 90,000 students annually for more than 50 districts with more than 2,300 vehicles. CVC DIF agreed to acquire the platform from Access Holdings through DIF Infrastructure VII on August 12, 2025, and Access described the sale as a successful exit by September 15, 2025. The exact legal close date, stake and acquisition vehicle below the fund are not publicly disclosed. Krise Transportation and Assisted Student Transportation are operating companies beneath ASTP, and Brandywine routes and vehicles are acquired assets rather than separate manager-level PortCos. No later platform sale or signed pending ownership transfer was identified through August 19, 2026.",
